package bool_as_f32;
// Bug: ECast int→float used SIToFPOp for bool (i1), making true as f32 = -1.0.
// Fix: i1 must use UIToFPOp (same as unsigned integers), giving true as f32 = 1.0.
// true as f32 = 1.0,  false as f64 = 0.0,  1 + 0 + 41 = 42
//
// ⚠ WHICH CLAUSE THIS FILE ACTUALLY PINS, MEASURED 2026-08-10. Until that day
// the int→float arm of `MLIRGenImpl::gen_expr_kind(ECastView, …)` carried TWO
// mutually redundant tests — an i1 test on the MLIR value and
// `LogosType::is_unsigned_repr_kind` on the Logos source type, which names
// `Kind::Bool` — so THIS FILE STAYED GREEN under the removal of either one and
// could only see the removal of both. The i1 clause is now deleted (the site
// carries the instrumented counts that licensed it), and this file is a
// single-clause sensor: excluding `Kind::Bool` at that arm alone gives
// `true as f32` = -1.0, so `x as i32` is -1 and main returns 40, not 42.
// PREDICTED 40, MEASURED 40. Its partner sensor is
// `tests/logos/pass/wql_agg_avg_bool_value_rule.logos` (exit 13 in the same
// build), which reaches the rule through a `deem` aggregate instead of a cast.

fn main() -> i32 {
    let x: f32 = true as f32;
    let y: f64 = false as f64;
    return x as i32 + y as i32 + 41;
}
